# Anchored with a leading slash wherever the intent is "the one at the root".
#
# A bare `assets` in gitignore matches a directory of that name at EVERY level,
# not just this one — so it silently swallowed src/shared/assets/catalog.ts,
# src/main/assets/scan.ts and src/main/assets/place.ts. They were never
# committed, nothing said so, and the first sign of it was CI failing to
# typecheck a module that exists perfectly well on the machine that wrote it.

node_modules/
/out/
/dist/
.DS_Store
*.log

# Python sidecar
sidecar/.venv/
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]

# The face-detector measurement venv (docs/CLIPS.md §4.1, §4.3): mediapipe
# installed --no-deps beside the pinned small packages, and the two BlazeFace
# model files under its models/. Rebuilt by hand per machine; never shipped.
sidecar/.venv-faces/

# The asset library: a real folder on the Mac (82M by `du -sh`, 88 fonts beside
# the SFX, titles, transitions and props; checked 2026-10-29). The Surface's
# checkout had no `assets` entry at all before the commit that added the four
# files below (checked 2026-10-29) and reads its library from the packs
# installed under userData; from that commit on it holds assets/fonts with
# just those four. Not a symlink on either: git cannot track a path beyond one,
# so a linked `assets` would refuse the four files below. The library is other
# people's work and stays uncommitted — but only THIS one, hence the slash.
#
# Except two fonts and their licences (docs/CLIPS.md §6.20, D10): Noto Sans
# Devanagari and Noto Sans Telugu, OFL, committed so CI's libass, the harness
# and every installer see the same Hindi and Telugu faces as a user's machine.
# They must sit in assets/fonts itself, since libass takes one fontsdir. Git
# cannot re-include a file inside an excluded directory, so the root's
# contents are excluded rather than the folder, then fonts/ is let back in and
# its contents excluded again, and the four files named.
/assets/*
!/assets/fonts/
/assets/fonts/*
!/assets/fonts/NotoSansDevanagari-Regular.ttf
!/assets/fonts/OFL-NotoSansDevanagari.txt
!/assets/fonts/NotoSansTelugu-Regular.ttf
!/assets/fonts/OFL-NotoSansTelugu.txt
/asset-catalog.json

*.tsbuildinfo

# Scratch left behind by tools handed ":memory:" as a database path. The colon
# makes the name illegal on Windows, and git cannot even check out a tree that
# contains one: `error: invalid path`, exit 128, before a single test runs.
*:memory:*

# The meme vault and the matted stickers — 2.7GB, and not ours.
#
# `Master_Viral_Meme_Vault` is the scraped originals; the `_COMPLETE` folder is
# the same set after background matting. They are source material for the
# sticker library, they are other people's footage, and together they are larger
# than every other thing in this repository by three orders of magnitude.
#
# Anchored, because the intent is these two at the root. Committing them once
# would be permanent: git history does not forget, and GitHub refuses a single
# file over 100MB. What the library NEEDS in the repo is the catalogue that
# describes them, never the footage itself — the same split /assets already
# makes.
/Master_Viral_Meme_Vault/
/Master_Viral_Meme_Stickers_COMPLETE*/

# Reference recordings — other people's work, kept for study.
#
# Instagram reels and app screen-recordings that features were measured
# against. They belong on this disk and not in a public repository: they are
# not ours to redistribute, and they are a hundred megabytes of video. What
# they TAUGHT us is written down in docs/REFERENCES.md, which is committed —
# so the findings survive even if the files do not.
/references/recordings/

# Per-machine tool permissions. The name says local; it differs on every
# machine and blocks a rebase every time it changes.
.claude/settings.local.json

# What the render checks rendered.
#
# The integration tests put their mp4s, their sampled frames and a README
# explaining each check into tests/output/<check>/ and LEAVE them there, so a
# failure can be looked at rather than only read about. It is rebuilt on every
# run and it is video, so it is evidence rather than source.
/tests/output/
